cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark or viewer, please cite it as below."
title: "shadowclock: can vision-language models read the time of day from overhead shadows?"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Bansal"
    given-names: "Maanvi"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-23"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A controlled benchmark of overhead (nadir) renders with exact solar ground truth, a pixel-based analytic baseline,
  results for three small open vision-language models, and a browser-based 4D sun viewer for twelve OpenStreetMap-derived
  city scenes. A negative result on weak models, reported with its limits.
keywords:
  - vision-language models
  - shadows
  - solar position
  - remote sensing
  - benchmark
  - geospatial
